WEBVTT

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:06.730
Riichi!

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:09.940
Pon.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.540
Ron. 1,300.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:25.560
Yes.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:29.820
<i>Another quick end to the hand...</i>

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.850
<i>In a game where winning one 
in four times is lucky as it is,</i>

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.300
<i>this gets rough...</i>

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.960
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.240
East Hand 3

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.240
Dealer: Takimi Haru

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:24.710
Tsumo.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:27.500
1,600. 3,200.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.840
I figured it was around there.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.360
<b>Hand 7: 
Attention</b>

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.250
<i>She was in tenpai?</i>

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.040
<i>She never declares riichi.</i>

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.280
<i>Her play records from the past 
were also always like that.</i>

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.200
<i>It's not as if she's as bad as Momo-chan,</i>

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.260
<i>since you just can't tell she's in tenpai,</i>

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.180
<i>but to me, she's still the biggest mystery here.</i>

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.640
East Hand 4

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.640
Dealer: Kakura Kurumi

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.980
I guess I'll declare riichi.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:52.830
Chi.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:55.900
That's it.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.900
Ron.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:01.160
So your thing is to end it with a 
cheap hand when someone's in tenpai?

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.410
It seemed to work on Kiyosumi,

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.540
but don't treat me the same way.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.540
I'm in a different league.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.920
Who cares? Just tell us the points you get!

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.260
It's 5,200.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.760
<i>It's always been hard to read 
the person from Himematsu.</i>

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:29.520
<i>The person from Kiyosumi has also been 
getting harder to read since the first half.</i>

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.020
It looks like Haruru is struggling a bit.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:36.790
She's doing her best to 
make it through the match.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:40.780
It looks like that's not really 
working with Himematsu.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.280
South Hand 1

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.280
Dealer: Takei Hisa

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:48.830
All right!

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:53.130
<i>Her confidence is amazing, 
but it's not just that.</i>

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.330
<i>She's the team captain at 
a prestigious Kansai school.</i>

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.180
<i>In last year's inter-high 
and the spring tournament,</i>

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.590
<i>she was the only one who 
always had a positive score.</i>

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:05.110
<i>She's got the results to justify her 
confidence. And she shows no hesitation.</i>

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.360
<i>Jealous doesn't even cover how I feel.</i>

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.940
<i>I'm not nervous anymore.</i>

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:12.850
<i>I'm getting back into my game, as well.</i>

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.190
<i>Still, it's not going as I'd like.</i>

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.560
<i>It's been a while.</i>

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.200
<i>Damn, this is fun!</i>

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.680
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.470
<i>Thanks, everybody...</i>

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:31.260
<i>for bringing me here.</i>

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.860
<i>It's been worth the various waits.</i>

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:40.590
<i>Maybe I should wait here as well.</i>

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.190
<i>I'm used to waiting, after all.</i>

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.560
South Hand 4

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.560
Dealer: Kakura Kurumi

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.320
South Player: Takei Hisa

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:08.530
<i>A live tile.</i>

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:10.700
Kan.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.410
<i>An open kan on a wind worth no yaku?</i>

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.920
<i>Four dora?!</i>

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.510
<i>She discarded a two-tile sequence with dora 
and had two possible ways to complete it...</i>

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.200
<i>Is she going for a character honitsu?</i>

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.770
<i>We finally get to see some characters.</i>

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.990
<i>And it's the red 5 that she just drew.</i>

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.420
<i>If she had an ittsuu,</i>

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.610
<i>she should've kept the red 
5 in the 4-5-6 sequence.</i>

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:52.100
<i>The honor tiles are out.</i>

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.000
<i>There are no 1 of circles left, so 
she can't have a sanshoku, either.</i>

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.750
<i>The most likely hand is a character honitsu.</i>

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.830
<i>If it's not that, it's a chanta!</i>

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:07.130
<i>Himematsu is wasting no time 
in copying the 5 of characters.</i>

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.830
<i>I can't call...</i>

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:10.190
Sorry.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:18.520
<i>Whether it's a chanta or a honitsu, 
this'll make it through!</i>

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.480
<i>No! She isn't that honest.</i>

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.610
<i>She's got bad manners.</i>

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:30.360
<i>She might have discarded the red 5 
and still have a normal 5 in her hand!</i>

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:34.080
<i>I'll play a safe tile here.</i>

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:41.630
Tsumo.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.040
3,000. 6,000.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.890
<i>It really was an ittsuu.</i>

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:48.920
<i>Why didn't she go for a honitsu?</i>

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.680
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 Third Player - 3rd Year
 Kakura Kurumi

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.680
Thank you.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.520
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 Third Player - 3rd Year
 Atogo Hiroe

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.520
Whew, it's over.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.940
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 Third Player - 1st Year
 Takimi Haru

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:59.940
Good game.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:03.690
Kiyosumi High School 
(Nagano)
 Third Player - 3rd Year
 Takei Hisa

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.400
Thank you.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.570
The third players' match is over!

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.090
The prestigious Himematsu

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:08.530
shoots from last place straight to first,

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.990
thanks to the performance 
of its ace, Atago Hiroe.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.700
She's the only one to finish with a positive score.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.180
In second place is Kiyosumi.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.160
In third is Miyamori, and in fourth is Eisui.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.710
All schools have fallen down one place.

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.560
Himematsu has taken the lead,

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.070
but the point differences from 
second place down are small.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.710
There's still plenty of potential for a storm.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:32.220
<i>Yes.</i>

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:36.520
<i>Near the last hand, I was able to 
play pretty much the way I'd hoped.</i>

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:39.480
<i>If I had been able to play like 
this from the beginning...</i>

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.480
<i>Well, no point in kicking myself.</i>

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:48.250
<i>At first, I was hesitant just 
to walk up to this chair...</i>

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:57.490
You guys aren't going back?

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:02.190
I'm not your child or grandchild,

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:05.720
so why don't you just let me be?

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:11.070
I just feel like sitting here for 
a bit longer. Weird, huh?

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:15.390
<i>Creepy.</i>

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.140
<b>Kiyosumi</b>

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:19.340
Captain's still not back...

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:22.390
There's no point in waiting, so I'll go now.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.350
Keep your head on straight.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.390
Good luck!

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:28.370
Tear 'em apart!

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:29.400
I will!

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:32.740
There she is!

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.990
It's Haramura Nodoka!

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:36.920
The champion of the 
inter-middle tournament!

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:39.590
Will her skill prove to be enough 
for the high school level?

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:44.250
Finally appearing in the inter-high, 
here's Haramura Nodoka!

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.000
Her first appearance, eh?

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.220
I was all prepared for her in the first match,

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:51.850
but it was all in vain since 
it ended after someone

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:53.460
got bumped out during 
the third players' match.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.680
I really hope to see something this time.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:00.160
But the teams that get adored 
like idols tend to lose, right?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.810
Like Karouto High School from Hiroshima.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:05.010
Expectations are riding on 
the fourth players' match.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:09.310
In the lower left of the screen is 
the time until the match begins.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.990
Haramura is so popular. I wonder why.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:16.610
The one that we need to pay 
attention to is less Haramura,

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.790
and more Eisui's Usuzumi.

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:22.040
Eisui's winning pattern in 
the prefectural preliminaries

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.160
was that Jindai and Usuzumi 
raked in the points

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.830
while Iwato shut out the opponents.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.720
Jindai's style varies,

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.340
as if she's testing out several play styles.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.380
But Usuzumi Hatsumi is strong, 
without any of that variation.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:38.890
Kinue-chan will have to do her best.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:41.390
I believe she will manage just fine.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:45.930
Hey, Kinu.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:46.600
Sis!

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.490
Well? I did it, right?

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:53.070
Yeah! That was amazing! 
We're at the top now!

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:57.480
Well, it was to be expected with my skill.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:59.030
Now it's your turn.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:00.530
Yep!

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:04.410
Good luck!

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:10.160
Kinu seemed tense or something.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:12.170
Will she be okay?

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.210
<b>Eisui Girls'</b>

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:17.880
All right, Princess. I'm off.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.720
We're 24,700 points behind first place.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:24.160
As the fifth player, it would really help me

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.860
if you could take care of that.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:29.100
Just leave it to me!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.270
<b>Eisui Girls'</b>

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:35.460
Will Eisui's Usuzumi make her appearance here?

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:39.560
She is just as attractive a player as Haramura.

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:44.280
Yes. Among Eisui's players, Jindai 
tends to get most of the attention,

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:47.620
but Usuzumi's high scores 
are noteworthy as well.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:50.870
Huh? She's not coming out.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.630
Here we have Haramura again!

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.220
It's Haramura-san!

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.370
We're lucky this time.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:07.030
Of the nine gods, Jindai Komaki 
had summoned a weaker one.

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:10.850
And thankfully, Usuzumi 
Hatsumi is the fourth player.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:13.430
This is just right for Sae.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:19.390
<i>We're in third place and 7,700 
points behind second place.</i>

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:23.590
<i>If we don't get to at least second place, 
we won't make it to the semifinals.</i>

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:27.870
<i>What's more, Eisui's Usuzumi 
Hatsumi is in fourth place.</i>

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:33.030
<i>I have to do everything 
I can to keep her there!</i>

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:50.550
Captain.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:52.950
Good work.

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:54.270
Oh, sorry.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.650
I leave the rest to you.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:58.810
Okay.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.290
That's Eisui's fourth player.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:15.850
You didn't know?

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:17.560
Of course not!

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:19.960
"I don't care about the other teams."

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:23.520
"I'm just going to do my best, 
regardless of who my opponents are!"

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.950
This happens because you say things like that.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.410
And he's down.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:53.660
Etopen!

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:54.760
Huh?

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.190
Oh, that was yours?

00:12:57.190 --> 00:13:01.340
Sorry! It kinda creeped me out, 
so I just... I'm sorry.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.290
He's okay!

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:09.810
Good.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:17.940
Ridiculous.

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:28.530
I'm really sorry!

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:32.390
Oh, no... He's fine, really, so...

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.350
It's not a matter of fine or not.

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:36.750
Right...

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:39.690
Has there been some kind of problem?

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:43.770
Himematsu's Atago Kinue is 
apologizing to Haramura,

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:47.400
but it seems like Haramura doesn't mind?

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.220
I suppose it's not an issue, then.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:53.450
I love the way they forgive each other. 
They're acting like true high schoolers.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:57.560
Kinu was a goalie in the 
middle school soccer club.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:00.310
Being kicked by someone like that can't be fun.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.560
Earlier, she was way too tense,

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:06.730
so if it got rid of some of that, 
I guess it's a good thing.

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:12.680
I'm sorry, too. I lost so many points...

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:18.770
Huh? Mahjong's a game where even 
the strongest players lose points.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:19.540
It's fine.

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:25.560
Right. Thank you.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.250
<i>Nodoka, I'm counting on you.</i>

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:32.120
<i>I hope that thought won't be corrupted.</i>

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.740
The fourth players' match will begin shortly.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:39.050
Playing for Eisui Girls' is 
third year Usuzumi Hatsumi.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:43.010
In the Kagoshima prefectural preliminaries, 
she broke regional records by wide margins.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:44.070
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 Fourth Player - 3rd Year
 Usuzumi Hatsumi

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:44.490
This player packs a lot of firepower!

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.320
Good luck.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:53.200
Himematsu High School's Atago Hiroe has 
passed the baton to her sister, Atago Kinue.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:49.280
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 Fourth Player - 2nd Year
 Atago Kinue

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.830
Good luck.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:57.460
Miyamori Girls' Usuzawa Sae

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.810
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 Fourth Player - 3rd Year
 Usuzawa Sae

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:01.810
shut down Makapi High School's 
Mekaru in the first round match.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:03.590
Good luck.

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:07.670
And from Kiyosumi High School: Haramura Nodoka.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.550
Kiyosumi High School 
(Nagano)
 Fourth Player - 1st Year
 Haramura Nodoka

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:10.800
Last year, she was the champion of the
inter-middle individual tournament.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.020
Good luck.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.770
I wonder what her strategy against these

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:18.680
older students from strong schools will be.

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:22.830
We've reached the climax:

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:24.950
the fourth players' match everybody 
will want to pay attention to

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:27.530
is now beginning!

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:36.080
South Player

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:36.080
Haramura Nodoka

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.580
<i>This is my first time playing</i>

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.650
<i>on the national level as a high schooler.</i>

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:42.580
<i>The difference from last year is that</i>

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:45.080
<i>my opponents are all older than me.</i>

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:55.680
<i>And if I lose, we'll all be separated...</i>

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:58.790
I'm sorry.

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:03.690
<i>Worrying won't do me any good. 
The only choice I have now...</i>

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:10.280
<i>is to do what I always do, as I always do.</i>

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.340
<i>Wings?</i>

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:31.210
<i>This is...</i>

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:35.260
<i>This is way earlier than 
Suehara-senpai said it would be!</i>

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:38.510
Touka! Nonoka's...

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:42.000
Yes. It seems she has awakened already.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.560
Good morning, Nodocchi.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:55.720
Show the entire nation what you are 
capable of, and hold nothing back!

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.620
<i>It feels like the atmosphere's changed a bit.</i>

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:08.630
<i>Kiyosumi's fourth player...</i>

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:11.500
<i>That's weird. Her face is red, too.</i>

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:14.470
<i>It looks like she's got a cold.</i>

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:17.480
<i>Even though this is just 
like Suehara-senpai said,</i>

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:19.400
<i>it still bothers me.</i>

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:22.460
<i>Her body temperature went up?</i>

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:25.980
<i>Nothing seems out of the ordinary, though...</i>

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:35.130
<i>Earlier, it seemed like something 
covered her for a moment.</i>

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:36.200
Pon.

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:41.650
<i>Is the shrine priestess collecting bamboo?</i>

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:44.910
<i>Bamboo's the dora... scary...</i>

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:47.610
<i>There's nothing more I want than to add</i>

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:49.920
<i>to the points my sister gathered,</i>

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.160
<i>but protecting these is my highest priority!</i>

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:55.420
Play in the team tournament?

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:59.250
I'm just a first year.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:03.200
Yes. It's just a fall tournament, 
not the inter-high.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.390
So no need to worry too much.

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:09.190
In the fall, we can switch 
around the order freely.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:12.150
You can experiment a bit 
in regional tournaments.

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:15.650
Then I'll try to not be too excited.

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:19.920
No, be excited. Your wish came true.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:28.820
<i>I see. I'll be able to play 
on the same team as my sister.</i>

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:35.030
The older sister who was 
admitted on a scholarship

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:37.300
after making a huge splash at 
the middle school tournaments,

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:41.370
and the younger sister who took general 
entrance procedures to follow her.

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:46.810
You've caught up a bit, Kinu-chan.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:57.490
<i>No, I'm still way behind!</i>

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:04.750
<i>Fall aside, I wasn't able to pull my weight 
at all in the spring tournament, either.</i>

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:07.290
<i>And after I was finally 
chosen as a starting member...</i>

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:11.290
<i>I can't accept that Himematsu is fine 
finishing fifth in the spring tournament.</i>

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:13.110
<i>If I had been better,</i>

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.870
<i>our team would have been much higher!</i>

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.220
<i>I'm going to contribute to this one!</i>

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.400
Riichi.

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:25.140
<i>As I say that, the dealer declares riichi!</i>

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:27.680
Tsumo.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.140
3,000. 6,000.

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:30.940
Huh? You?

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:35.550
<i>I couldn't feel any offensive aura, 
or any power, for that matter.</i>

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:37.270
<i>She just won.</i>

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:42.950
<i>Almost like she's a machine or something... 
like she's not even human.</i>

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.920
Nonoka won the hand!

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:48.200
Yes, anything less wouldn't 
be Haramura Nodoka.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.350
It's a haneman.

00:19:50.350 --> 00:19:52.830
That was a pretty smooth win...

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:56.990
That's indeed Haramura Nodoka's style,

00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:00.840
but I feel like she immediately 
shifted into top gear.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:07.890
<b>Kiyosumi High School (Nagano)
 Fourth Player - 1st Year
Haramura Nodoka</b>

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:04.410
<i>In the prefectural preliminaries, 
Haramura in this state</i>

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:07.210
<i>had basically perfect tenpai efficiency.</i>

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:10.410
<i>However, I believe it took quite some time</i>

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:12.600
<i>for her to reach this state back then.</i>

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:15.660
<i>Did she improve that in 
preparation for the nationals?</i>

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:19.070
East Hand 2

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:19.070
Dealer: Haramura Nodoka

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:23.640
Ron!

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:25.950
3,900.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:27.450
Yes.

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:31.790
<i>All right. I took some 
points from second place.</i>

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:35.540
East Hand 3

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:35.540
Dealer: Usuzumi Hatsumi

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:39.250
No tenpai.

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:40.540
No tenpai.

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:41.460
Tenpai.

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.050
No tenpai here.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:01.190
East Hand 4

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:01.190
Carried Bonus 1

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.740
Dealer: Atago Kinue

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:09.870
<i>Now...</i>

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:13.120
<i>Eisui is the north player...</i>

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:19.250
<i>All right, Usuzumi is the north player.</i>

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:22.300
<i>Good luck, Kinu-chan.</i>

00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:29.590
It's time, isn't it?

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:30.510
Yes.

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:57.500
<i>My monocle fogged up. 
I guess that means it's coming.</i>

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:12.680
<i>All right, come get some, 
shrine priestess of Akuseki!</i>

00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next time:</b>

00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Fortress</b>

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:39.160
What's the probability of getting a suushiihou?

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:39.160
[Suushiihou: Three each of all four winds, or 
three each of three winds plus a pair of the fourth]

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:40.530
About 1 in 10,000.

00:23:40.530 --> 00:23:43.770
Roughly the same chance as an 
amateur golfer getting a hole in one.

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:44.940
Incidentally, if it's a pro,

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:46.270
it's the same chance as getting a daisangen.

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:48.360
I have to tell our captain!

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:55.250
<b>Please watch
next
time!</b>
